{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JbWoi67cKrb7egKatfuP2P","type":"tool_result","content":"1234180 my-3d2dge.js\n  16336 session.js\n1250516 total\n/*!\n * my-3D2dge v0.85.1  (My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine)\n * Procedural pixel-puppet engine for every 2D perspective.\n * https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge  (MIT License)\n *\n * READ THIS FIRST (humans and AI models extending a my-3D2dge game)\n * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * 0. EVERY GAME STARTS WITH  const E = My3D2dge;  and then uses E.Game, E.px, ...\n * 1. WORLD SPACE IS 3D. x = east, y = south, z = up. One floor tile = 16 units.\n *    Game logic never thinks about screen pixels.\n * 2. A VIEW turns world points into screen pixels. Swap th\n836:      if (e.pointerType === 'mouse' || this._fingers.size === 1) this._gesture('down', ...this.screenPoint(e.clientX, e.clientY), { touch: e.pointerType !== 'mouse', button: e.button, id: e.pointerId }); else this._g = this._gBox = null;   // (a second finger: a pinch, no gesture)\n1090:  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\n1096:    if (!o.touch) this._fedAt = [x, y];\n1097:    const S = this.screen, z = o.touch && type === 'down' && this.zones && this._zone(x / S.W, y / S.H);\n1099:    if (o.touch && type === 'up' && this._zoneOf.has('fed' + (o.id || 0))) { this._zoneUp('fed' + (o.id || 0)); return; }\n1100:    if (type === 'down') { this._fed = [x, y]; if (!o.touch) this.press('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._gesture('down', x, y, { touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, id: 'fed' }); }\n1104:      if (!o.touch) this.release('Mouse' + (o.button || 0)); this._fed = null; this._gesture('up', x, y);\n1111:    if (type === 'down') { this._g = { id: o.id, x0: x, y0: y, x, y, t: this.clock, touch: !!o.touch, button: o.button || 0, mode: null, long: false, moved: false }; return; }\n2663:   * - view, views, input, res, expand, touch: a scene's, applied when it starts: input ('PLATFORMER'), res ('snes'),\n3001:  touch: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Touch buttons', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Automatic'], ['on', 'Always'], ['off', 'Hidden']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\n3002:  hand: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Buttons on', type: 'select', value: 'right', options: [['right', 'Right'], ['left', 'Left']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\n10598:  runs. Touch: a tap walks; a tap on a hotspot opens its verbs; the inventory by taps, a thumb's size; a long press\n14133:Touch: a tap selects or orders, a drag on open ground pans (game.cam.free), a long press and a drag draws a box, a pinch\n789:    /** glyphs: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' |\n792:    this.glyphs = 'auto'; this.rumbleScale = .6; this.padLost = false;\n895:   *  button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family) */\n904:  /** the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says */\n906:    if (this.glyphs && this.glyphs !== 'auto') return this.glyphs;\n1302: * 6. PIXEL FONT  3x5 glyphs for in-world numbers and labels\n1354:  normal: { glyphs: parseFont(G57), h: 7, desc: 2, gap: 1, space: 3, upper: false },\n1355:  tiny: { glyphs: parseFont(GLYPHS), h: 5, desc: 0, gap: 2, space: 3, upper: true, mono: 3 }\n1369:  _glyph(f, ch) { return f.glyphs[f.upper ? ch.toUpperCase() : ch] || f.glyphs[ch.toUpperCase()] || f.glyphs['?']; },\n1372:    for (const ch of line) w += ch === ' ' ? f.space + 1 : (f.mono || this._glyph(f, ch).w) + 1;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"812255b0-ea3a-4ee3-85b0-07e0e895a85a","uuid":"1d523c4c-1a8e-4968-8209-28477a09b332","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:15:05.905Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1234180 my-3d2dge.js\n  16336 session.js\n1250516 total\n/*!\n * my-3D2dge v0.85.1