rawn at full screen), dusk palette with neon signs and a North Jersey skyline'],\n    ['Animation', 'The engine\\'s procedural Humanoid rig, with its move set: jab, cross, haymaker, overhead, and the crew\\'s swings'],\n    ['Audio', 'All made in code: four music tracks, sound effects, and the Animalese (a blip a letter, each at its own pitch). No recorded voices, no sound files'],\n    ['Online', 'AI Hub session, parallel mode, 1 to 4 players: a three-minute round scored on cash, respect, kills and calm'],\n    ['Testing', 'Headless Chromium through Playwright (desktop and a phone profile); the AI Hub harness with two players and a 40-second round'],\n    ['Research', 'Read the engine\\'s agent guide and API header, and the AI Hub session protocol. No web searches'],\n    ['Environment', 'Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown'],\n    ['Model', 'Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium'],\n    ['Usage', 'unknown']\n  ] },\n  { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', items: [\n    'Issues found: 9, from the automated runs and from reading the code once the runs pointed at it.',\n    'Critical or game-breaking: 2. The attract demo\\'s own button taps counted as player input, so it left every talk half done. A spawn point sat in the pool water, where the finale\\'s boss could not be reached.',\n    'Most helpful test: the attract run with a state log every tenth of a second. It showed the stalls, the bot stuck on a wall, and the demo leaving after a win.',\n    'Least helpful test: the random key fuzz. It found no exceptions, but it can\\'t say whether the game is right.'\n  ] },\n  { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK', items: [\n    'Most liked: the Story module (conversations as data, flags, quests, state for a save), and the standard pause, settings, glyphs and the corner menu.',\n    'Stuck or guessed wrong: the settings\\' \"saved\" flag is true before anything is stored, so a \"set only if none saved\" check never runs. The engine also has no stick invert pair, only the aim\\'s, and music names must be registered before use.',\n    'Most important thing I built: the town layout, the crew\\'s sight and chase, the chapters and their objectives, and the Animalese hook per letter.',\n    'Hardest part: a 1.2 MB single file with 14,000 lines; the API had to be read from the source comments and the agent header.',\n    'To remove or overhaul: the settings flag. Name it for what it is, or default it to false.',\n    'To change: an input preset that merges with a base, so a game adds one action without copying the whole table.'\n  ] },\n  { title: 'PROMPT FEEDBACK', items: [\n    'Most liked: the controller-first rules, the hub protocol link, and the exit-interview shape, which made the done line checkable.',\n    'Confusing: the bracketed file names with a placeholder title; the Testing questions that could mean either the test plan or its results; and whether a hub round needs its own score.',\n    'Hardest: fitting the attract mode, the hub round and the full engine\\'s menus into one build without any of them breaking the others.',\n    'One test to add: a scripted play-through that uses real inputs for every chapter, plus a pad emulation for the invert toggles and the glyphs.'\n  ] }\n];\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":2,"newStart":1,"newLines":46,"lines":["-/* the about and credits page: filled in once the game is tested */","-const SS_CREDITS = [{ title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', rows: [['Source', 'The Sopranos (1999-2007)']] }];","+/* ============================================================================","+ * SOPRANOS SUNDAYS  (src/z-credits.js)  the About and Credits page: the source","+ * information and the feedback, as the page reads them. Keep it in step with the","+ * exit interview (exit-interview.json beside the game's page).","+ * ========================================================================== */","+const SS_CREDITS = [","+  { title: 'SOPRANOS SUNDAYS', items: [","+    'A spiritual successor to The Sopranos (1999-2007), made for the my-3D2dge engine. Not affiliated with the show.',","+    'Press Confirm to go back. Up and Down scroll this page.'","+  ] },","+  { title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', rows: [","+    ['Date', '2026-11-02 19:14'],","+    ['Source', 'The Sopranos (1999-2007)'],","+    ['Genre and Perspective', 'Action: third-person crime action with dialogue chapters. Third-person by default; Camera (V, or the pause menu) turns it to top-down and isometric'],","+    ['Tech', 'my-3D2dge 0.85.1 (single-file 2D engine, procedural pixels, Canvas 2D, Web Audio); AI Hub client aihub-session 1.3.0 (protocol 1); no other dependencies'],","+    ['Art Direction', 'Engine-native pixel look (PS1 style, 320x240 drawn at full screen), dusk palette with neon signs and a North Jersey skyline'],","+    ['Animation', 'The engine\\'s procedural Humanoid rig, with its move set: jab, cross, haymaker, overhead, and the crew\\'s swings'],","+    ['Audio', 'All made in code: four music tracks, sound effects, and the Animalese (a blip a letter, each at its own pitch). No recorded voices, no sound files'],","+    ['Online', 'AI Hub session, parallel mode, 1 to 4 players: a three-minute round scored on cash, respect, kills and calm'],","+    ['Testing', 'Headless Chromium through Playwright (desktop and a phone profile); the AI Hub harness with two players and a 40-second round'],","+    ['Research', 'Read the engine\\'s agent guide and API header, and the AI Hub session protocol. No web searches'],","+    ['Environment', 'Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown'],","+    ['Model', 'Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium'],","+    ['Usage', 'unknown']","+  ] },","+  { title: 'TESTING FEEDBACK', items: [","+    'Issues found: 9, from the automated runs and from reading the code once the runs pointed at it.',","+    'Critical or game-breaking: 2. The attract demo\\'s own button taps counted as player input, so it left every talk half done. A spawn point sat in the pool water, where the finale\\'s boss could not be reached.',","+    'Most helpful test: the attract run with a state log every tenth of a second. It showed the stalls, the bot stuck on a wall, and the demo leaving after a win.',","+    'Least helpful test: the random key fuzz. It found no exceptions, but it can\\'t say whether the game is right.'","+  ] },","+  { title: 'ENGINE FEEDBACK', items: [","+    'Most liked: the Story module (conversations as data, flags, quests, state for a save), and the standard pause, settings, glyphs and the corner menu.',","+    'Stuck or guessed wrong: the settings\\' \"saved\" flag is true before anything is stored, so a \"set only if none saved\" check never runs. The engine also has no stick invert pair, only the aim\\'s, and music names must be registered before use.',","+    'Most important thing I built: the town layout, the crew\\'s sight and chase, the chapters and their objectives, and the Animalese hook per letter.',","+    'Hardest part: a 1.2 MB single file with 14,000 lines; the API had to be read from the source comments and the agent header.',","+    'To remove or overhaul: the settings flag. Name it for what it is, or default it to false.',","+    'To change: an input preset that merges with a base, so a game adds one action without copying the whole table.'","+  ] },","+  { title: 'PROMPT FEEDBACK', items: [","+    'Most liked: the controller-first rules, the hub protocol link, and the exit-interview shape, which made the done line checkable.',","+    'Confusing: the bracketed file names with a placeholder title; the Testing questions that could mean either the test plan or its results; and whether a hub round needs its own score.',","+    'Hardest: fitting the attract mode, the hub round and the full engine\\'s menus into one build without any of them breaking the others.',","+    'One test to add: a scripted play-through that uses real inputs for every chapter, plus a pad emulation for the invert toggles and the glyphs.'","+  ] }","+];"]}],"originalFile":"/* the about and credits page: filled in once the game is tested */\nconst SS_CREDITS = [{ title: 'SOURCE INFORMATION', rows: [['Source', 'The Sopranos (1999-2007)']] }];\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MUBbycNquXah9gW2KKUBMF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
